<td style="width: 80%;">Increases the damage done by your <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47811/immolate">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_immolation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Immolate</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47813/corruption">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_abominationexplosion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corruption</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47843/unstable-affliction">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_unstableaffliction_3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unstable Affliction</span></a> spells by 10%.</td></tr></tbody></table>All the different <a class="icontiny c9" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/warlock">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warlock.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warlock</span></a> specializations benefit from both Tier 9 set bonuses. The two-piece bonus results in our favorite demons having more juicy critical hits, overall this isn't the most impactfull increase. When it comes to the four-piece bonus all specializations utilize one or multiple of the buffed spells <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47811/immolate">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_immolation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Immolate</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47813/corruption">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_abominationexplosion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corruption</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47843/unstable-affliction">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_unstableaffliction_3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unstable Affliction</span></a> in their rotation, this is overall the more impactfull benefit. There are three versions of tier gear this phase.<br/>
<br/>The strongest variant, 258-item level version is rewarded from completing Heroic 25 man <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a> and can be bought with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47557/regalia-of-the-grand-conqueror">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_chain_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Regalia of the Grand Conqueror</span></a>. These items are some of the strongest available this phase, even purely stat wise ignoring the set bonus benefits. However, they are also hard to get, seeing as only 2 to 4 of all the Regalia (including for other classes) drop per instance depending on the number of attempts left after defeating <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a> on Heroic difficulty.<br/>
<br/>The second-best option, which you will likely be wearing and using before you get your heroic pieces is the normal 25-man 245-item level pieces. These pieces often are the second best available for the item slot, if not for the stat for the fact that they provide us a step closer to our four-piece set bonus. These can be bought from a combination of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47242/trophy-of-the-crusade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trophy_argent.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Trophy of the Crusade</span></a> and <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=301/emblem-of-triumph">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></span></a>. Of note is that both <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47242/trophy-of-the-crusade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trophy_argent.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Trophy of the Crusade</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47557/regalia-of-the-grand-conqueror">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_chain_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Regalia of the Grand Conqueror</span></a> can be used to buy the item slot piece of your choosing (in comparison to needing a specific item for each item slot).<br/>
<br/>The last version of the set can be bought with only <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=301/emblem-of-triumph">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></span></a> but has significantly less stats due to being only item level 232. On top of that you cannot upgrade towards the 25-man version, in other words you will need to spend a significant amount of extra <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=301/emblem-of-triumph">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></span></a> if you go this route.<br/>
<br/>You will have to <a href="https://wowsims.github.io/wotlk/warlock/" target="_blank">simulate</a> your setup to determine which upgrades and pieces make the most sense to get first as a lot of this will depend on your current equipment. Alternatively, you can also look over at the results from the <a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13C9JBs4RaHAkOe-Go9wGnv5CORm11qH6n1EQwnwx-zE/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank">Warlock Simulation Competition</a> to see various setups and how they fare compared to the absolute best in slot setup.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="gems">Gems</h4>For gemming, you will want to use these slots to balance out your Hit and reach your meta gem requirement. Most often it is not worthwhile to get the gem bonus unless it is a spell damage, hit, or haste bonus. For more in-depth info on gems, see the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/warlock/destruction/dps-enchants-gems-pve">Gem Guide.</a>
