<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Warlock DPS in Phase 3</h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="head">Head</h3>One of arguably the most important slots for achieving our four-piece set bonus from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-176/triumphant-guldans-regalia">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Triumphant Gul'dan's Regalia</span></a> is the head. It makes the biggest jump in performance if we give up on the head slot and instead opt for using a non-tier piece here. Luckily this phase we can choose in which order we get our tier pieces as we can buy them using either <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47557/regalia-of-the-grand-conqueror">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_chain_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Regalia of the Grand Conqueror</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47242/trophy-of-the-crusade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trophy_argent.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Trophy of the Crusade</span></a> combined with <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=301/emblem-of-triumph">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></span></a>. In general, it is also recommended to simulate your specific gearing upgrade path when it comes to tier 9, sometimes it will be more beneficial to upgrade another slot first if you didn't get luck on your side last phase. However, most often the tier 9 helm will be the biggest tier piece upgrade available. <br/>
<br/>If you already have <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45497/crown-of-luminescence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_99.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crown of Luminescence</span></a> from phase 2, it will be able to hold itself up until you get either of the 25-man versions of the Tier 9 helm. All other headpieces perform roughly equal or worse compared to it. Note that if you do not utilize the head slot to reach your four-piece bonus you will want to equip one of the Tier 9 chest variants (Note that the chest slot is the only place where non-tier pieces outperform the 25-man heroic tier option).<div class="box">
<b>Head Enchant</b>: <a class="q7 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50368/arcanum-of-burning-mysteries">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_masterofelements.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of Burning Mysteries</span></a> &gt; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44075/arcanum-of-dominance">
