<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="rings">Rings</h3>In comparison to the previous Phase, we have a lot of close worthwhile options instead of a clear winner combination. Talking about Phase 2 both <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45495/conductive-seal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_66.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conductive Seal</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46046/nebula-band">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_70.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nebula Band</span></a> (which can now be bought for 19 <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=2589/sidereal-essence">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_icediamond_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sidereal Essence</span></span></a>) hold up incredibly well. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47489/lurid-manifestation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_55.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lurid Manifestation</span></a> is the new kid on the block, it ends up being one of the best available rings.<br/>
<br/>Most of the other rings listed all perform incredibly close to each other. Another thing of note would be the hit rating. Most of the best rings do not have any hit rating on them, the exception being <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45297/shimmering-seal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_63.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shimmering Seal</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48001/firestorm-band">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_57.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Firestorm Band</span></a>. Both should be considered if you need additional hit rating and do not have one of the other hit-specific items mentioned throughout the guide.<br/>
<br/>Also of note is the newly upgraded <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48957/etched-signet-of-the-kirin-tor">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_73.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Etched Signet of the Kirin Tor</span></a>, costing a further 1000g on top of the hefty 8000g cost of the Phase 1 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44935/ring-of-the-kirin-tor">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_74.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of the Kirin Tor</span></a>. It performs relatively well, in the middle of the pack of great rings. Certainly worth considering depending on your luck in Phase 2 with rings.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47439/circle-of-the-darkmender">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_80.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Circle of the Darkmender</span></a> is technically an upgrade over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47732/band-of-the-invoker">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_54.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of the Invoker</span></a> but with the stronger alternatives available to <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warlock.gif");'></span>
<span class="c9">Warlocks</span> this should be left for the healers, at least if you still want to get topped off after a <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=57946/life-tap">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_burningspirit.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Life Tap</span></a> session.<div class="box">
<b>Ring Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44636/enchant-ring-greater-spellpower">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Ring - Greater Spellpower</span></a> (<a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=333/enchanting">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchanting</span></a>).</div>
